bruce spanner and natasha romanov have a  complicated history  from that scary chase scene to that  infamous heart to heart  here are the biggest black widow and  hulk scenes in the mcu  ranked from best tourist the best scene  between natasha romanov and  bruce banner might just be their first  it comes in the avengers when natasha  has been tasked with recruiting bruce to  the team  at the time bruce is on the land living  in kolkata and working as a medical  doctor  he shows up at what he believes to be  the home of a patient but instead he  finds agent romanov waiting for him  bruce is immediately on edge and he asks  if the building is surrounded but widow  is calm  and casual assuring him that they're  alone she tells bruce that she's come to  recruit him for his scientific expertise  smiling nervously bruce muses that  perhaps she's come to lock him up which  widow denies  finally bruce slams down his fists and  shouts  stop me at this natasha becomes deadly  serious and draws a hidden gun  it's now clear that natasha has been  absolutely terrified of bruce this  entire time but was hiding it like a  champ  something further underlined by the  reveal that shield agents had the  building surrounded the entire time  it's a tense and beautifully constructed  scene that also  manages to quickly teach us everything  we need to know about these two  characters moving forward  bruce is trying to achieve balance  between his two halves and doesn't want  to be caged  natasha is excellent at hiding her  feelings and  she's far deadlier than she seems on top  of all that it's mark ruffalo's first  real scene playing banner and he totally  knocks it out of the park  another of our favorite moments between  hulk and widow comes at the end of  avengers age of ultron in a scene that's  arguably the final resolution of their  romantic subplots though we didn't  know it at the time after defeating  ultron the avengers are fleeing the  floating chunk of sokovia where they  took their stand against the killer  robot  although most of the team including  black widow escaped aboard a shield  helicarrier  the hulk opted for a different way off  the island flying away in a stolen  quinjet  as he flies further and further away  from the rest of the team  natasha pops up with a video message  with visible concern and longing on her  face  she pleads with him to turn the plane  around instead hulk terminates the  message  and sits in silence as the quinjet flies  off into the unknown  it's a beautiful little scene that we  enjoy in large part because of its  simplicity  bruce never wanted to be an avenger in  the first place and now he has a chance  to disappear forever  his only regret is that he won't get  seen that again and  all of this is clear on both of their  faces without either of them  saying a word another hulk in black  widow scene that we simply adore  comes early in age of ultron as the  avengers celebrate victory over hydra  back at stark tower  natasha is pouring some drinks behind  the bar and bruce walks up to her and  things get a little flirty it begins  with pleasant banter as bruce uses an  old movie lean to get natasha to play  along  as their flirtation continues though  natasha essentially confesses that she  has feelings for bruce and tries to get  a sense of whether or not he feels the  same way  since bruce is a huge dork though he's  less skilled at this sort of banter and  he fails to give nats the answer she's  looking for  this moment is a big shift in their  relationship when their simmering  romance officially transitions from  subtext  to text though this romantic pairing  took many audiences by surprise during  their initial viewing of this film  it's a genuinely great little  interaction the two have some real  chemistry and it's nice to see two  sombre characters having a little fun  also it's a little thing but we love the  fact that widow being a veteran super  spy  is way better at flirty role playing  than the awkward and  uptight banner all in all this scene is  a delight  when loki's forces launch a surprise  attack against the shield helicarrier in  the avengers  an explosion sends bruce and natasha  tumbling down into the aircraft's lower  decks  natasha finds her leg pinned under some  debris and bruce  overwhelmed by his stressful  surroundings starts to turn green  by the time natasha frees herself and  starts limping away bruce has become the  hulk  from there a tense chase scene ensues as  an injured widow  struggles to run and hide from a monster  that used to be her ally  this little horror interlude is a really  cool scene and it's a nice tonal  contrast with bruce and natasha's usual  flirtations  that being said we don't love the fact  that during this sequence in which  all the rest of the avengers get to do  cool stuff the lone  female member of the team is relegated  to getting injured running away from a  monster and then spending the rest of  the sequence cowering in the storage  room  before finally getting rescued by thor  after losing a few points for that  this scene is still pretty great overall  after their tearful goodbye at the end  of age of ultron  hulk in widow's romantic subplot is more  or less dropped from the series moving  forward  there is however a little nod to their  past entanglement in avengers infinity  war when the team is reassembling in  order to make a stand against thanos  after spending several years as a  fugitive when black widow finally  rejoins the team  she finds an unexpected person waiting  for her back at avengers hq  during bruce and natasha's brief  interaction it's immediately clear that  the pair still have a great deal of  affection for one another but it's also  clear that neither one is entirely sure  of where they stand or what they want  from each other  the two never get to have another big  heart to heart at least  not one that we see and they spend the  rest of the film fighting against thanos  rather than patching things up  we wish the scene could be a bit longer  and that it gave us a resolution to this  particular plot line but  infinity war is such a dense film that  we imagine the filmmakers just didn't  have time for it  that being said what we do get here is  still pretty great  so this awkwardly sweet scene stands out  among the bruce natasha moments  here's the scene we have mixed feelings  about from age of ultron natasha has  been captured by ultron and bruce  arrives to save her  he frees her from her jail cell and  tries to convince her to leave with him  but she wants to stay in fight  we cut away for a bit and see that  ultron has begun his final plan  to levitate a section of scovia up into  the sky when we return to bruce and  natasha he tries again to convince her  to leave with renewed vigor instead  natasha does  this i adore you after the kiss  she pushes him into a pit a moment later  the hulk leaps up from the abyss below  and lands in front of natasha grinning  and ready for action  this scene isn't higher on our list  because it's an example of a time when  the writers want to have it both ways  they want to show the audience that  after everything he's gone through bruce  is genuinely traumatized and he no  longer wants to be the hulk  at the same time though for the climax  of their big superhero movie  they want the good guy version of hulk  to be involved punching robots and stuff  their way of accomplishing both these  goals is to have natasha  non-consensually transform an unwilling  bruce  it's fine but it's also sort of a cheap  gotcha twist and  it's played entirely for laughs in a way  that doesn't really acknowledge that  this is a genuinely awful thing for nat  to do to bruce  who really doesn't want to be the hulk  anymore after the team breaks through  the defenses of a hydra base it's time  for the avengers to reassemble and head  home  however since the hulk is still  rampaging around in the woods natasha  sent out to calm him down  and it's here that we get to see the  first appearance of the team's new  technique for de-hulking the hulk  the lullaby hey big guy  sun's getting real low with the gentle  caress of the hulk's palm and forearm  after uttering this code phrase  natasha seems to immediately calm the  hulk down then  after a moment the big guy backs away  and collapses to the ground  transforming back into a shirtless  banner honestly we can't really decide  how we feel about this scene it's sort  of a cool idea that widow has the  ability to help calm down the hulk and  get him to transform back into banner  but the whole scene has a sort of  uncomfortable energy to it that just  doesn't work for us we're not really  sure what director joss whedon was  thinking with this one but if he was  going for  sexy he very much missed the mark it  seems like perhaps even some of the  other folks at marvel also weren't  super big fans of this somewhat awkward  scene as it was later turned into a  punchline in thor ragnarok  despite their long history black widow  and the hulk share barely  any screen time during their final film  together avengers endgame  natasha's storyline focuses much more on  her relationship with hawkeye  and bruce's time is split between  reconnecting with thor and  doing science stuff that being said the  pair do have one brief interaction  together early on in the film when  natasha  stevens got to meet bruce at a diner we  learned that the big guy has now merged  his two halves hulk  and banner into a single being banner  explains that one reason he decided to  do this was because he personally blames  himself for the team's loss to thanos  there's no flirting but natasha does  make some time to comfort bruce  and to compliment him when he worries he  might not have the expertise to figure  out time travel  well you pulled this off i remember a  time when that seemed pretty impossible  too  the scene is more of a group moment but  it's worth mentioning because believe it  or not  it's the last time we get to see hulk  and widow have a real conversation  it's a perfectly fine scene the only  reason we're ranking it so low is  because of how anticlimactic this  ends up being as the pair's last true  interaction  after a lost ultron that included an  accidental hulk rampage the team decides  to lay low at hawkeye's rural family  home  while they're there natasha decides to  make her play she asks bruce to run away  with her but he refuses saying  she's out of her mind his reasoning he  feels that being the hulk means he can't  have a normal relationship with her  and he can't have kids she responds by  telling him she can't either  and that the red room that trained her  also had her sterilized  it's efficient  one less thing to worry about perhaps  there's a version of this scene that  could have worked we'd love to see more  of widow and hulk talking about how they  both feel like monsters who don't fit in  that whole dynamic is the main reason  why they work so well as  pairing but in this specific execution  the writers tried to convey this idea in  a truly tasteless way by having both of  them lament their infertility  presumably without realizing it the  scene basically implies that people who  can't have kids are unfit to be in a  relationship  and that they're well monsters even if  it wasn't the intended message  this complete catastrophe of a scene  clearly gets the bottom spot  on our list with a bullet check out one  of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite superhero movies are coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one  [Music]
 

